  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Varun Beverages Ltd vs State Of Rajasthan on 2 July, 2021",
    "facts": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the petitioners were found guilty of violation of sub-section 2(ii) of Section 26 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'the Act of 2006) read with Food Safety and Standards (Food Products Standards and Food Additives) Regulations, 2011 and as (2 of 2) [CW-6751/2021] such they were directed under Section 52 to pay fine of Rs. 2,00,000/-. Learned counsel submitted that the petitioners have filed an appeal under Section 70 of the Act of 2006 before the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal, Jaipur and at present no person is holding the post of Presiding Officer in the Appellate Tribunal and as such, appeal of the petitioners is not taken up.",
    "arguments": "",
